Z||000000||fropuff||08-22-2001||11:47 PM||||Hey guys.  My car seems to be running crappier than usual.  I've really noticed it about two weeks ago up until now.  First of all, my gas mileage is worse than usual.  I'm getting 140/tank, where as my "usual" was around 170.  And I'm not even pushing it that hard.  Secondly, I'm getting pretty bad acceleration lag from a stopped take-off.  Even when I slightly power-brake, it still does it.  My 0-60 times are also significantly worse than before.  Tonight, I raced my brother, in two different cars.  I was suprised at the outcome of the two.  The first was with a '98 Taurus wagon (3.0L).  Before, I used to waste him.  Now, I can barely beat it.  And it's around a 9.5 second 0-60 car.  The second was with his '92 GP SE (3.1L).  I used to beat him pretty bad, but now I just keep up.  He beats me to 60, but then we stay side-by-side until 100.  Then I take him.  And it's around an 8.5-9 second 0-60 car.  8.5 seconds 0-60 sounds normal for my car (auto), but the acceleration is bad in general.  What can I do to remedy this crappiness?  I'm going to do nitrous this winter, but I want to make my car run good first.  Thanks for any help!!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||fropuff||08-22-2001||11:49 PM||||BTW: The car is an '86 GT w/ the 2.8L engine and 3-speed auto tranny.  Thanks again!||||reg||1
